P(0) in this particular case is 0.71 so it is not extraordinarily low (for whales).

It is counter-intuitive for me because if I had estimated p(0) independently and used it as a multiplier, it would be impossible for the corrected estimate cv to be lower than that for the uncorrected estimate (I think...).

